    You get out the word just in time, queuing in <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Thomas</span> the fact that you are the culprit. <span style="color:LightGreen">His fist stops a mere inch from your face, causing you to release his underwear and nearly fall to the ground in relief.</span> That was way too close. <br>
    <br>
    <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“<span style="color:DarkTurquoise">$ThomasNickname</span>?”</span> He says in surprise, his confusion quickly turning to anger as his face becomes bright red. <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“What the hell are you doing!? I almost knocked you out you- you-!”</span> He growls in anger as he fixes his underwear glaring at you. You apologize, your heart still beating rapidly, and say you were just trying to be funny. But now that you think about it, probably not the best idea. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Thomas</span> continues to glare at you for a moment before he sigh and his arms relax. <br>
    <br>
    <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“You’re so lucky I like you.”</span> He says under his breath. <span style="color:Pink">You smirk and ask him to repeat that</span> <span style="color:yellow">when he suddenly holds his fist up to you, causing you to jump back.</span> <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Try that again, and my fist is going up your ass!”</span> <span style="color:Pink">You can’t help but smirk at the unintentional lewdness of his threat. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Thomas</span>, realizing this, blushes once more and quickly turns around to walk away.</span> <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Nevermind, I do hate you.”</span> <br>
